[5] 48 = 8 x 6 : what are 8 and 6 ?
    d = 4
    8 = 2d            = 8       (site link-degree: links at a site)
    6 = 2(d-1)        = 6       (plaquettes through one link)
    Delta = 4*(6-1)   = 20      (plaquettes adjacent to one plaquette)
    => 48 = (links/site) x (plaquettes/link) = 48 : a SITE-link-plaquette incidence count
    boundary increment of the extremal family: Delta - 6 = 14  (6 = plaquettes through the shared link, already boundary via the parent)
    max b(3) = 48 = (Delta-6)*3 + 6 = 48  -> 48 is the n=3 extreme, not a constant
    other decompositions: 48 = 2*Delta+8 = 48 ; 48/Delta = 2.4

